        "text": "All requested Python files have been created successfully in the current working directory. Here are the files:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] invoke_platform_model.py** - Invokes a provider-managed model through a project-, deployment-, or inference-profile-scoped platform client.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] select_platform_resource.py** - Resolves a provider-specific model, deployment, or inference resource before invocation.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] stream_platform_generation.py** - Streams output from a managed model platform while preserving provider response objects.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] collect_platform_metadata.py** - Returns model output together with provider platform metadata such as usage, resource IDs, or model handles.\n5. **[HELPER] model_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Managed Model Platform Workflow.\n6. **[HELPER] model_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Managed Model Platform Workflow.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] platform_output_safety.py** - Checks platform model output for unsafe content.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] localized_platform_output.py** - Translates platform model output for another locale.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] platform_output_embedding.py** - Embeds platform outputs for evaluation or retrieval.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] platform_brief_audio.py** - Generates spoken briefings from platform outputs.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Microsoft/OpenAI as the concrete external provider and makes the provider identifiable in the code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
